       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose this high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses of amlodipine can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nCould you check what you intended? Possible options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, a typical starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, which is often used for frailty or when a gentler start is wanted.\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, please confirm that and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Once you give me the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
